ce\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d88\"},\"ref\":\"d88\",\"snippet\":\" ... Barry Keoghan\\n\\nBORN: October 18, 1992\\n\\nBIRTHPLACE: Dublin, Ireland\\n\\nCHILD: Brando\\n\\nASTROLOGICAL SIGN: Libra\\n\\nEarly Life\\n\\nBarry Keoghan was born on October 18, 1992, and raised in the Summerhill neighborhood of Dublin. Keoghan had no relationship with his father, whose identity hasn't been made public. His mother ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.biography.com/actors/a46180093/barry-keoghan\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d89\"},\"ref\":\"d89\",\"snippet\":\" ... Michael Joseph Jackson\\n\\nBORN: August 29, 1958\\n\\nDIED: June 25, 2009\\n\\nBIRTHPLACE: Gary, Indiana\\n\\nSPOUSES: Lisa Marie Presley (1994-1996) and Debbie Rowe (1996-2000)\\n\\nCHILDREN: Michael \\\"Prince,\\\" Paris, and Prince \\\"Blanket\\\"\\n\\nASTROLOGICAL SIGN: Virgo\\n\\nEarly Life and Family\\n\\nMichael Joseph Jackson was born on August 29, 1958 ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.biography.com/musicians/michael-jackson\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"b00ad6a509a10aa1beb993153db57804082175527b0a43fe0475d64c8338ac4b\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"78d04a0bebd0cc3f7947a3b3fdedc9e02fef8e9dc40785581d8bf78e0ed20949\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Marlon James birthplace born city\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e1\",\"start\":0}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d21\"},\"ref\":\"d21\",\"snippet\":\" ... Program Director\\n\\nChigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationaler Literaturpreis, FT/Oppenheimer prize ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d15\"},\"ref\":\"d15\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2015 | Shortlist | Tom McCarthy | Satin Island | Jonathan Cape | * Michael Wood (chair) * John Burnside * Sam Leith * Frances Osborne * Ellah Wakatama Allfrey |\\n| 2015 | Shortlist | Chigozie Obioma | The Fishermen | One | * Michael Wood (chair) * John Burnside * Sam Leith * Frances Osborne * Ellah Wakatama Allfrey |\\n| 2015 | Shortlist | Sunjeev Sahota | The Year of the Runaways ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d90\"},\"ref\":\"d90\",\"snippet\":\" ... Arrow of God (1964), No Longer At Ease (1960), Things Fall Apart (1958), A Man of the People (1966), Anthills of the Savannah (1987), \\n* Chimamanda Ngozi Adichie (Nigeria): Purple Hibiscus (2003), Half of a Yellow Sun (2006), Americanah (2013)\\n* Chigozie Obioma (Nigeria): The Fishermen (2015), An Orchestra of ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/African_literature\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d37\"},\"ref\":\"d37\",\"snippet\":\" ... This book brilliantly explores the effects of slavery and colonialism on African families as the story unfolds between West Africa and the United States.\\n\\n- The Fishermen (2015) by Chigozie Obioma (Nigeria): In this heartbreaking tale, four brothers in a small Nigerian town have their lives turned upside down ... \",\"title\":\"https://enkoeducation.com/the-must-read-in-african-literature/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d36\"},\"ref\":\"d36\",\"snippet\":\" ... Chigozie Obioma\\ndate: 2000-01-01\\n---\\n-\\n\\n- MajorsMinorsCertificates\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Policies & ProceduresFYW Guidebook\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Digital Learning LabsPortfoliosEvaluationsMoran ePortfolio AwardsBarnett Essay AwardsDouble Dawgs\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Transfer FAQProspective Student Information\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Study AbroadInternships and Research Opportunities\\n\\n>>\\n\\n-\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Double DawgsTransfer Student InformationDual Degree Progra\",\"title\":\"https://www.english.uga.edu/directory/people/chigozie-obioma\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"c210bc73b7e81e4da0c7d8bce6f46a9d3abcfd42222ad24db3de9d5935e42251\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"8a6bad53844ad8c16f0ea05c03223950f969908c5aaf33135a1b70b3f89467c1\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"The Fishermen Chigozie Obioma 2015 Booker Prize shortlist\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_1869fb06b4f6484f901acad1"},{"content":"I have a strong lead. From e1, I've confirmed:\n- Chigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria\n- His novels \"The Fishermen\" (2015) and \"An Orchestra of Minorities\" (2019) were shortlisted for the Booker Prize and translated into 30 languages (over 25 ✓)\n\nNow I need to verify the puzzle's structure. The puzzle says the award was \"originally created in the 2000s.\" The Booker Prize was created in 1969, which doesn't fit. But the puzzle might be using loose phrasing, OR there's a different interpretation. Let me reconsider: \"An Orchestra of Minorities\" (2019) was a Booker contender. In 2019, the Booker was won by \"The Testaments\" (Atwood) and \"Girl, Woman, Other\" (Evaristo). \n\nBut wait — the puzzle says Book B \"had been released the preceding year\" and won the award in the year Book A was published. \"The Testaments\" was published in 2019 (same year), not preceding. Let me reconsider whether the puzzle refers to the regular Booker or International Booker, and check the 2019 Booker winner details and whether any winner was published the preceding year.\n\nLet me also reconsider: maybe Book A is \"The Fishermen\" (2015), and in 2015 the Booker was won by \"A Brief History of Seven Killings\" (Marlon James, published 2014 — the preceding year!). Let me verify this and Marlon James's birthplace.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"A Brief History of Seven Killings Marlon James publication date 2014 Booker Prize 2015\", \"Marlon James birthplace born city\", \"The Fishermen Chigozie Obioma 2015 Booker Prize shortlist\"]}","name":"search"},"id":"call_56635095e220497cb31eb959","index":0,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":true,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d43\"},\"ref\":\"d43\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://www.ontheprize.co.uk/blog/the-booker-prize-in-the-2010s\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d82\"},\"ref\":\"d82\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://www.grinnell.edu/campus-life/arts-culture/writersgrinnell/distinguished-authors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d14\"},\"ref\